**Date:** 1 November 2026 · **Proposed by:** Nathan2128 · **Replaces:** [0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject), once accepted

## Context

[0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges reports whose subject lines match. Under
it, #4471 collected reports of [three different problems](/kb/incidents/4471-split): the
parser, the booking-v3 date hint, and dates that move by one day. The subjects did not follow
the problem: the same subject turns up under all three. One ticket, one fix queued, and two
of the problems had no owner.

## Decision

Two reports are the same issue when they have the same cause. The cause comes from the
report's tenant (locale and booking form) and channel, as `causes.ts` runs it, plus what the
desk reads in the body for problems the tenant can't show (`desk-notes.json`). The subject
line is not used.

## Consequences

- Triage reads a little more: tenant and channel are on every report; the body only when
  the date moved by one day.
- A cause that has no ticket yet gets one, instead of joining the biggest ticket nearby.
- The [triage page](/kb/triage/dedupe) still describes 0001 and needs rewriting if this is accepted.

